1
00:00:00,270 --> 00:00:02,200
[The characters, behaviors,
locations, organizations, professions,

2
00:00:02,220 --> 00:00:04,150
and events depicted in this series are entirely fictional

3
00:00:04,170 --> 00:00:06,100
and created for entertainment purposes only.

4
00:00:06,120 --> 00:00:08,050
No harm or illegal action is intended
to be promoted or encouraged.

5
00:00:08,070 --> 00:00:10,000
Viewer discretion is advised]

6
00:00:10,910 --> 00:00:12,080
Damn it, Jaab!

7
00:00:12,100 --> 00:00:13,720
Why did I fall for him?!

8
00:00:13,740 --> 00:00:14,680
Do you like Jane?

9
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:16,200
Who's Jane?

10
00:00:16,240 --> 00:00:17,030
Oh, Mek?

11
00:00:17,050 --> 00:00:17,700
What brings you here?

12
00:00:17,720 --> 00:00:19,360
But I'm actually surprised that

13
00:00:19,380 --> 00:00:20,920
a goofball like you

14
00:00:21,130 --> 00:00:23,000
is serious about a relationship.

15
00:00:23,250 --> 00:00:25,440
I've never imagined that

16
00:00:25,870 --> 00:00:28,040
I'd have another close friend aside from Min.

17
00:00:28,170 --> 00:00:31,040
If she finds out, she must be really happy for you.

18
00:00:32,750 --> 00:00:34,040
Jane.

19
00:00:34,470 --> 00:00:35,480
I...

20
00:00:36,890 --> 00:00:37,890
like...

21
00:00:40,280 --> 00:00:41,600
Auntie Kaew! Auntie Kaew!

22
00:00:41,620 --> 00:00:42,520
Yes?

23
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:45,600
- Ow!
- Auntie Kaew!

24
00:00:46,920 --> 00:00:47,920
Master Jaab,

25
00:00:47,940 --> 00:00:51,000
you're amazing. You're the best.

26
00:00:51,020 --> 00:00:51,920
Auntie Kaew,

27
00:00:52,010 --> 00:00:53,800
let me know
how many more you need.

28
00:00:53,820 --> 00:00:55,720
I'll pick them for you right away.

29
00:00:55,790 --> 00:00:58,160
Can I ask for one more?

30
00:00:58,320 --> 00:00:59,200
Just one more lime?

31
00:00:59,230 --> 00:00:59,960
One more orchard.

32
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:01,590
- Huh?! An entire orchard?!
- Mm.

33
00:01:01,610 --> 00:01:02,470
Yes, the whole orchard.

34
00:01:02,490 --> 00:01:03,720
Once we're done with the limes,

35
00:01:03,740 --> 00:01:05,710
I’ll have you pick some marian plums

36
00:01:05,740 --> 00:01:07,190
from those two orchards over there.

37
00:01:07,210 --> 00:01:10,100
Then come back here
for some plum mangoes.

38
00:01:10,120 --> 00:01:11,400
Oh, what a shame.

39
00:01:11,420 --> 00:01:12,670
Longans aren't ready just yet.

40
00:01:12,690 --> 00:01:14,340
We would've had more fun

41
00:01:14,370 --> 00:01:15,520
going through
four or five orchards of them.

42
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:18,360
It's a shame, really.

43
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:20,440
I was just joking!

44
00:01:21,640 --> 00:01:23,080
Auntie Kaew!

45
00:01:23,310 --> 00:01:25,640
You're quite a funny person, huh?

46
00:01:26,620 --> 00:01:28,160
I was joking about the longans.

47
00:01:28,310 --> 00:01:30,890
But I'm serious about
the lime orchard.

48
00:01:31,300 --> 00:01:32,200
- Huh?
- Here.

49
00:01:32,220 --> 00:01:33,690
You've only picked one lime.

50
00:01:33,710 --> 00:01:35,360
Come on.
Let's get to it.

51
00:01:35,380 --> 00:01:36,220
- Then...
- But Auntie Kaew...

52
00:01:36,240 --> 00:01:38,370
- Come on.
- I've only managed to pick one.

53
00:01:38,390 --> 00:01:39,660
Get started with it.

54
00:01:39,680 --> 00:01:41,350
Just snip, snip,
and snip those stems away.

55
00:01:41,370 --> 00:01:43,280
Just a few quick snips
and you're done.

56
00:03:18,160 --> 00:03:19,520
How is it?

57
00:03:20,430 --> 00:03:21,470
Auntie...

58
00:03:21,960 --> 00:03:23,650
This mango is delicious.

59
00:03:23,900 --> 00:03:25,160
It's perfectly sweet and sour.

60
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:26,540
I think this one is better.

61
00:03:26,560 --> 00:03:27,920
- Try it.
- Alright.

62
00:03:31,170 --> 00:03:31,960
Mm!

63
00:03:32,190 --> 00:03:33,560
This one hits the spot,

64
00:03:33,620 --> 00:03:35,950
but the one before tastes better.

65
00:03:35,970 --> 00:03:37,200
Right.

66
00:03:37,320 --> 00:03:38,470
Oh, Auntie Kaew,

67
00:03:39,380 --> 00:03:40,500
I'm curious.

68
00:03:40,670 --> 00:03:43,570
Jane told me his family owns some orchards,

69
00:03:43,590 --> 00:03:45,280
but I don't know
what kind of orchards they are.

70
00:03:45,460 --> 00:03:46,860
Many kinds of fruits are grown here.

71
00:03:47,460 --> 00:03:49,480
Mister and Madam...

72
00:03:50,920 --> 00:03:52,640
Master Jane's parents, I mean.

73
00:03:52,980 --> 00:03:55,840
They inherited this plot of land

74
00:03:56,080 --> 00:03:57,720
which stretches from this mountain

75
00:03:57,860 --> 00:04:00,460
all the way to another...

76
00:04:00,480 --> 00:04:01,360
Whoa, whoa.

77
00:04:01,780 --> 00:04:03,370
That's enough, Auntie.

78
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:04,130
You can stop now.

79
00:04:04,150 --> 00:04:05,560
Does the land really stretch that far?

80
00:04:05,770 --> 00:04:07,940
Are you pulling my leg again?

81
00:04:09,120 --> 00:04:10,970
I'm being honest with you.

82
00:04:11,910 --> 00:04:14,970
The reason Master Jane
never told you about this

83
00:04:15,210 --> 00:04:17,880
is probably because
he couldn't count them all.

84
00:04:20,270 --> 00:04:21,630
He couldn't count
all the mountains in the land?

85
00:04:21,650 --> 00:04:22,360
Right.

86
00:04:22,670 --> 00:04:24,920
And the rambutan, mangosteen,
and the durian orchards

87
00:04:25,060 --> 00:04:27,130
are on that mountain.
You need to drive to get there.

88
00:04:27,360 --> 00:04:28,070
Whoa.

89
00:04:28,090 --> 00:04:29,880
The ones that you can easily walk to

90
00:04:29,900 --> 00:04:32,610
- are the lime orchards you just saw.
- Oh...

91
00:04:32,910 --> 00:04:34,060
Oh, there's also

92
00:04:34,170 --> 00:04:36,250
a sweet tamarind orchard
in the backyard.

93
00:04:36,270 --> 00:04:37,530
There are all kinds of fruits here?

94
00:04:37,550 --> 00:04:39,040
There's a macadamia orchard, too.

95
00:04:39,150 --> 00:04:42,100
But we have to drive a long way
up a mountain.

96
00:04:42,590 --> 00:04:43,300
Oh.

97
00:04:45,160 --> 00:04:45,920
My lord.

98
00:04:46,560 --> 00:04:49,460
If I’ve offended or bothered you,

99
00:04:49,680 --> 00:04:50,680
please...

100
00:04:50,960 --> 00:04:52,320
spare me.

101
00:04:56,360 --> 00:04:57,760
My lord.

102
00:04:58,460 --> 00:05:00,880
Please enjoy
these fruits that Auntie Kaew

103
00:05:01,260 --> 00:05:02,330
and I...

104
00:05:02,350 --> 00:05:04,660
have harvested
with our own hands. Please.

105
00:05:05,420 --> 00:05:06,480
Whoa, hold up.

106
00:05:08,060 --> 00:05:09,540
You must not get your hands dirty.

107
00:05:09,560 --> 00:05:11,360
Here. Allow me to feed you.

108
00:05:11,920 --> 00:05:14,240
Fresh off the tree.
But it might be a bit salty.

109
00:05:14,260 --> 00:05:16,600
It's the saltiness from my hands.
Now, please.

110
00:05:25,880 --> 00:05:26,690
How is it?

111
00:05:26,920 --> 00:05:27,710
It's exquisite, right?

112
00:05:27,730 --> 00:05:29,380
Right. I've been eating this
since childhood.

113
00:05:29,400 --> 00:05:30,740
Yeah, I forgot.

114
00:05:30,760 --> 00:05:32,360
But I picked this one myself.

115
00:05:32,380 --> 00:05:33,730
The first one I've ever picked

116
00:05:33,960 --> 00:05:34,900
in my life.

117
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:36,380
Here. One more bite.

118
00:05:41,180 --> 00:05:42,180
Jane.

119
00:05:42,760 --> 00:05:44,070
You really grew these yourself?

120
00:05:44,760 --> 00:05:45,890
I thought you could
only find them overseas.

121
00:05:47,440 --> 00:05:48,880
They've been here for ages,

122
00:05:49,190 --> 00:05:50,680
even before I was born.

123
00:05:51,560 --> 00:05:53,400
They just have a fancy name.

124
00:05:53,870 --> 00:05:55,260
That's why people like you

125
00:05:55,850 --> 00:05:57,080
are often mistaken.

126
00:05:57,340 --> 00:05:57,990
Hey.

127
00:05:58,550 --> 00:05:59,970
What do you mean by that?

128
00:05:59,990 --> 00:06:00,720
Huh?!

129
00:06:03,480 --> 00:06:04,320
You...

130
00:06:04,860 --> 00:06:06,320
Are you calling me stupid?

131
00:06:06,460 --> 00:06:08,770
Oops. Did I accidentally
say it out loud?

132
00:06:09,370 --> 00:06:10,370
You...

133
00:06:11,880 --> 00:06:13,670
There!

134
00:06:14,870 --> 00:06:16,200
Jaab, you teased me again.

135
00:06:16,320 --> 00:06:18,080
Well, you made fun of me first.

136
00:06:18,170 --> 00:06:20,120
I was just thinking it.
I didn't say anything.

137
00:06:20,140 --> 00:06:21,080
There!

138
00:06:21,100 --> 00:06:23,240
You admitted it yourself
that you wanted to roast me.

139
00:06:25,360 --> 00:06:28,070
I was born and raised in Bangkok.

140
00:06:28,090 --> 00:06:29,470
My house only has fences.

141
00:06:29,670 --> 00:06:30,910
There's only a simple lawn in my backyard,

142
00:06:30,930 --> 00:06:32,560
and a few random trees Mom planted.

143
00:06:32,750 --> 00:06:34,270
Who could ever be as talented

144
00:06:34,290 --> 00:06:36,850
and as knowledgeable

145
00:06:36,870 --> 00:06:39,400
as you who can enjoy the starry sky
whenever you want?

146
00:06:40,020 --> 00:06:40,770
Huh?

147
00:06:43,920 --> 00:06:44,660
Hey.

148
00:06:45,140 --> 00:06:46,140
Be honest.

149
00:06:46,460 --> 00:06:47,800
Your life here is so comfortable.

150
00:06:48,470 --> 00:06:50,670
Why did you move to Bangkok
to work for someone else?

151
00:06:54,500 --> 00:06:55,640
I just wanted to see

152
00:06:56,060 --> 00:06:58,320
what a starless night sky looked like.

153
00:06:59,580 --> 00:07:00,980
A starless night sky...

154
00:07:01,670 --> 00:07:03,120
is just a sky.

155
00:07:03,910 --> 00:07:05,000
It's ugly.

156
00:07:05,480 --> 00:07:07,150
The sky here is much more impressive.

157
00:07:09,990 --> 00:07:11,720
A starry night sky

158
00:07:12,020 --> 00:07:14,360
might feel special to some people,

159
00:07:15,380 --> 00:07:16,980
but the things that
feel ordinary to them

160
00:07:17,680 --> 00:07:19,800
might also feel special to me.

161
00:07:22,660 --> 00:07:25,000
I grew up with all the things
people might consider special.

162
00:07:26,190 --> 00:07:27,640
I live in a big house.

163
00:07:28,120 --> 00:07:29,780
I have massive orchards.

164
00:07:30,790 --> 00:07:32,560
I get to see starry night skies.

165
00:07:35,110 --> 00:07:36,440
But to me...

166
00:07:37,220 --> 00:07:39,220
getting to experience something new,

167
00:07:40,420 --> 00:07:42,310
moving into a condo,

168
00:07:42,330 --> 00:07:44,160
living in a high-rise,

169
00:07:44,860 --> 00:07:46,880
working with a lot of people,

170
00:07:47,750 --> 00:07:51,260
and being in such a chaotic
and loud environment,

171
00:07:52,580 --> 00:07:54,920
all of these make my life
a lot more fun.

172
00:07:56,060 --> 00:07:58,360
I've been in my own shell since forever.

173
00:07:59,400 --> 00:08:02,840
Deciding to enroll in
a university on my own

174
00:08:03,550 --> 00:08:04,550
felt like...

175
00:08:05,170 --> 00:08:06,920
moving to a whole new world

176
00:08:07,840 --> 00:08:09,350
that I'd never known before.

177
00:08:11,280 --> 00:08:13,670
Even now, I must thank myself
for being brave.

178
00:08:14,660 --> 00:08:16,340
What I’ve gained from all this

179
00:08:17,560 --> 00:08:18,860
is very valuable to me.

180
00:08:21,870 --> 00:08:23,840
That includes
getting to know you, Jaab.

181
00:09:29,470 --> 00:09:30,960
I'm also happy

182
00:09:31,340 --> 00:09:32,640
that I got to know you, Jane.

183
00:10:25,540 --> 00:10:26,480
What are you doing?

184
00:10:31,820 --> 00:10:33,800
You woke up and immediately
started messing around, Jane?

185
00:10:42,320 --> 00:10:43,800
You look funny like this, alright?

186
00:10:44,050 --> 00:10:44,880
Well...

187
00:10:45,280 --> 00:10:46,640
My body was doing its own thing.

188
00:10:46,660 --> 00:10:48,200
I don't know
how I ended up like this.

189
00:10:50,760 --> 00:10:52,300
Next time, just ask.

190
00:10:52,320 --> 00:10:55,450
I told you there are plenty of
isolated corners here.

191
00:10:55,470 --> 00:10:57,150
So that you won't have to lie around.

192
00:10:58,570 --> 00:11:00,240
Jeez.

193
00:11:01,240 --> 00:11:03,010
You were snoring in your sleep.

194
00:11:03,030 --> 00:11:04,390
Who would have the guts
to wake you up?

195
00:11:04,420 --> 00:11:05,050
Ow!

196
00:11:05,070 --> 00:11:06,960
It was you who were snoring.

197
00:11:07,050 --> 00:11:09,180
Ow, Jane. Why did you hit me?

198
00:11:09,200 --> 00:11:11,350
That hurt. I think you just broke my arm.

199
00:11:11,370 --> 00:11:13,050
I can't work now.

200
00:11:14,760 --> 00:11:16,250
Hey, where are you going?

201
00:11:18,750 --> 00:11:19,760
Hey, Jane.

202
00:11:20,450 --> 00:11:21,730
You just woke up,

203
00:11:21,750 --> 00:11:22,940
and you're taking a nap already?

204
00:11:23,850 --> 00:11:24,950
It's my day off.

205
00:11:24,970 --> 00:11:26,040
What else do you want me to do?

206
00:11:33,240 --> 00:11:34,240
Of course.

207
00:11:34,560 --> 00:11:36,310
It's just me

208
00:11:36,470 --> 00:11:38,080
who has to work remotely.

209
00:11:39,070 --> 00:11:39,760
Jaab.

210
00:11:40,250 --> 00:11:40,990
Hm?

211
00:11:42,030 --> 00:11:43,600
Is it nice...

212
00:11:45,450 --> 00:11:46,480
having an older brother?

213
00:11:46,750 --> 00:11:47,840
Why did you ask?

214
00:11:51,010 --> 00:11:52,480
I'm just curious.

215
00:11:52,950 --> 00:11:55,080
Would it be nice to have one?

216
00:11:55,700 --> 00:11:57,800
And would it feel just like
what I imagined?

217
00:11:57,960 --> 00:12:00,140
Jeng and I are
eight years apart.

218
00:12:00,600 --> 00:12:02,860
That's pretty far apart
for a pair of siblings.

219
00:12:04,330 --> 00:12:06,250
But being eight years older

220
00:12:06,840 --> 00:12:08,330
allowed Jeng to

221
00:12:08,350 --> 00:12:10,350
become Mom's golden boy

222
00:12:10,740 --> 00:12:12,560
and gave him
all the company's work.

223
00:12:14,530 --> 00:12:15,600
You mean J. Group?

224
00:12:15,820 --> 00:12:16,710
Uh-huh.

225
00:12:17,630 --> 00:12:18,630
It's a good thing, though.

226
00:12:19,040 --> 00:12:21,040
I don't want that kind of job.

227
00:12:21,730 --> 00:12:24,000
I have to thank Jeng
for being born before me.

228
00:12:24,150 --> 00:12:25,540
That's why I've been allowed to

229
00:12:25,740 --> 00:12:27,880
live such a messy life.

230
00:12:27,990 --> 00:12:28,830
Yeah.

231
00:12:28,850 --> 00:12:31,640
So my final answer is that

232
00:12:32,440 --> 00:12:33,240
it's nice to have one.

233
00:12:33,550 --> 00:12:34,820
It's so freaking nice.

234
00:12:36,750 --> 00:12:37,750
Even though...

235
00:12:38,040 --> 00:12:39,920
he complains so much
as if he's my other dad,

236
00:12:40,160 --> 00:12:41,450
the good still outweighs the bad.

237
00:12:42,040 --> 00:12:43,680
So I'm cool with it.

238
00:12:44,060 --> 00:12:45,600
It's just like I thought, then.

239
00:12:45,720 --> 00:12:46,310
You...

240
00:12:47,530 --> 00:12:48,720
Are you alright, Jane?

241
00:12:56,280 --> 00:12:57,280
Jaab.

242
00:12:57,320 --> 00:12:59,080
See that orchard over there?

243
00:12:59,350 --> 00:13:00,340
Mm.

244
00:13:00,450 --> 00:13:01,660
You mean...

245
00:13:01,960 --> 00:13:03,550
from this mountain

246
00:13:03,570 --> 00:13:06,040
all the way to that one?

247
00:13:06,080 --> 00:13:07,110
Mm. There.

248
00:13:07,130 --> 00:13:08,830
All of that

249
00:13:08,850 --> 00:13:10,060
belongs to me.

250
00:13:10,550 --> 00:13:11,480
Whoa?!

251
00:13:11,520 --> 00:13:13,450
So you're a tycoon.

252
00:13:13,470 --> 00:13:15,820
Jeez, and I thought you took me here
to do something with me.

253
00:13:15,840 --> 00:13:17,120
You just wanted to brag.

254
00:13:18,980 --> 00:13:20,720
I mean...

255
00:13:22,140 --> 00:13:23,440
In the future,

256
00:13:24,150 --> 00:13:26,520
everything here will become
my responsibilities.

257
00:13:29,070 --> 00:13:30,650
The orchards,

258
00:13:30,850 --> 00:13:32,000
the workers,

259
00:13:32,150 --> 00:13:33,150
the plots of land,

260
00:13:33,930 --> 00:13:35,080
and...

261
00:13:37,340 --> 00:13:39,750
Dad's resort project
that will open soon.

262
00:13:40,930 --> 00:13:43,950
I have to take care of
everything myself.

263
00:13:47,840 --> 00:13:49,360
How will I handle them all?

264
00:13:53,440 --> 00:13:54,640
Hey, Jane.

265
00:13:56,420 --> 00:13:57,840
Are you okay?

266
00:13:58,290 --> 00:13:59,640
Do you know that...

267
00:14:00,240 --> 00:14:01,640
since the day I was born,

268
00:14:02,040 --> 00:14:04,760
my parents have spoiled me?

269
00:14:05,480 --> 00:14:06,960
Whatever school I wanted to go to,

270
00:14:07,140 --> 00:14:09,200
whatever I wanted to do
or to have as my own,

271
00:14:09,750 --> 00:14:10,920
they let me have everything.

272
00:14:12,250 --> 00:14:13,880
But it was like buying time.

273
00:14:14,540 --> 00:14:17,080
Eventually, I’ll have to
come back and work here.

274
00:14:23,150 --> 00:14:24,560
I'm jealous of you.

275
00:14:25,960 --> 00:14:27,440
Say...

276
00:14:28,060 --> 00:14:28,920
it'd be nice

277
00:14:29,250 --> 00:14:31,020
to have a brother like you do,

278
00:14:31,940 --> 00:14:33,080
right?

279
00:14:39,320 --> 00:14:41,920
If you want an older brother,

280
00:14:42,240 --> 00:14:44,860
I can find you one.

281
00:14:49,740 --> 00:14:50,880
Oh, but...

282
00:14:51,380 --> 00:14:52,960
He needs to help my dad
with the orchards.

283
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:54,680
I want somebody strong.

284
00:14:57,140 --> 00:14:58,850
I'm super jacked.

285
00:14:59,050 --> 00:15:00,950
I can carry tons of mangoes.

286
00:15:01,830 --> 00:15:02,830
But...

287
