552
00:29:22,540 --> 00:29:25,330
You two were alone together for two nights.

553
00:29:25,360 --> 00:29:26,600
Did you do anything
that might have

554
00:29:27,240 --> 00:29:28,640
ignited the romance?

555
00:29:29,450 --> 00:29:30,560
I don't know.

556
00:29:30,720 --> 00:29:33,200
I actually feel that way all the time.

557
00:29:34,960 --> 00:29:35,960
On your own?

558
00:29:36,140 --> 00:29:39,040
I'm talking about Jane.

559
00:29:39,170 --> 00:29:41,700
Did Jane do something
that made you go...

560
00:29:42,430 --> 00:29:44,040
like, "What the hell?!"

561
00:29:44,060 --> 00:29:45,700
Or did he make you
question yourself like, "Huh?!"

562
00:29:46,420 --> 00:29:50,020
Like something we never did
after being friends for a decade?

563
00:29:50,040 --> 00:29:50,680
Did he?

564
00:29:51,030 --> 00:29:53,800
Something we never did?

565
00:30:06,060 --> 00:30:07,320
- Khanoon.
- Hm?

566
00:30:07,680 --> 00:30:09,560
I don't want to get my hopes up.

567
00:30:10,600 --> 00:30:11,540
Hey.

568
00:30:11,840 --> 00:30:14,040
You're overthinking it.

569
00:30:14,250 --> 00:30:15,300
You're overthinking...

570
00:30:15,940 --> 00:30:17,840
so much that your tiny little brain

571
00:30:18,000 --> 00:30:20,040
is now overloaded.

572
00:30:21,820 --> 00:30:24,040
But Jane...

573
00:30:24,240 --> 00:30:25,560
Pun!

574
00:30:25,990 --> 00:30:27,530
How many times
have I told you to shut up?

575
00:30:29,560 --> 00:30:30,330
Hey...

576
00:30:30,360 --> 00:30:32,810
So you and I are in the same boat, huh?

577
00:30:32,830 --> 00:30:35,470
From now on, if I tell you to "go left,"
then you must go left.

578
00:30:35,490 --> 00:30:37,420
If I tell you to "go right,"
then you must go right.

579
00:30:37,450 --> 00:30:39,160
You must be a good supporter.

580
00:30:39,540 --> 00:30:40,540
Understood?

581
00:30:40,560 --> 00:30:41,440
Okay.

582
00:30:41,620 --> 00:30:42,400
Excellent.

583
00:30:42,550 --> 00:30:44,480
Are you done chatting?
Bew told me to fetch you.

584
00:30:50,350 --> 00:30:52,840
I was gonna tell you
that Jane was walking toward us.

585
00:30:52,870 --> 00:30:53,620
I wasn't gonna say that

586
00:30:53,640 --> 00:30:54,610
you have a crush on...

587
00:30:54,630 --> 00:30:56,250
- Hey! Ow.
- Stop! Stop it!

588
00:30:56,270 --> 00:30:57,170
We were...

589
00:30:57,190 --> 00:30:58,690
- talking about something...
- No... I mean, yeah.

590
00:30:58,710 --> 00:31:02,210
- Uh... About cryptocurrency.
- Cryptocurrency.

591
00:31:02,230 --> 00:31:03,660
- Yeah, yeah.
- It was completely green.

592
00:31:03,680 --> 00:31:05,000
- He's right... Hey.
- Correct.

593
00:31:05,020 --> 00:31:07,300
- Would you like to join us, Jane?
- Exactly.

594
00:31:07,330 --> 00:31:09,100
Pun, our dear brother,
wants to discuss it.

595
00:31:09,120 --> 00:31:11,120
- So the three of us are talking.
- Right. He wants money more than we do.

596
00:31:11,140 --> 00:31:12,080
He’s desperate for cash.

597
00:31:14,370 --> 00:31:17,200
This is Ai.
Today is his first day of internship here

598
00:31:17,230 --> 00:31:18,440
as a PD.

599
00:31:19,530 --> 00:31:22,000
- Hello, my name is Ai.
- Hi.

600
00:31:22,570 --> 00:31:23,330
Alright.

601
00:31:23,540 --> 00:31:24,670
That's Jane.

602
00:31:24,700 --> 00:31:28,750
He’s the nicest PD on the team.

603
00:31:28,780 --> 00:31:31,600
You're very lucky to work with him.

604
00:31:32,010 --> 00:31:33,430
Oh, Sis.

605
00:31:33,930 --> 00:31:34,930
What about me?

606
00:31:35,050 --> 00:31:36,600
Am I not your good boy?

607
00:31:36,820 --> 00:31:39,000
- Sheesh.
- Since when did I stop being your best boy?

608
00:31:40,030 --> 00:31:40,930
And that is...

609
00:31:40,960 --> 00:31:42,600
Chomphoo, one of the assistants.

610
00:31:42,820 --> 00:31:44,240
- Hi, dear.
- Hello.

611
00:31:44,760 --> 00:31:46,520
This is our director, Jaab.

612
00:31:46,720 --> 00:31:48,520
- Hi there.
- Hello.

613
00:31:48,910 --> 00:31:49,840
That's Pun.

614
00:31:50,240 --> 00:31:51,240
Hello.

615
00:31:51,750 --> 00:31:53,020
Hi.

616
00:31:53,040 --> 00:31:54,120
I'm Pun.

617
00:31:54,150 --> 00:31:55,600
Right. Hi.

618
00:32:00,240 --> 00:32:03,320
This is pretty much most of our team.

619
00:32:03,540 --> 00:32:05,960
And we outsource people for support.

620
00:32:07,020 --> 00:32:08,700
- What the hell?
- Oh.

621
00:32:08,720 --> 00:32:10,220
What about me?!

622
00:32:10,240 --> 00:32:14,160
I'm the best DOP on the pink team!

623
00:32:14,410 --> 00:32:15,410
Well, there.

624
00:32:15,530 --> 00:32:18,600
You've already introduced yourself.
I have nothing left to say now.

625
00:32:18,660 --> 00:32:20,820
- She's right.
- My introduction isn't as fancy as the others.

626
00:32:20,850 --> 00:32:22,790
- It's Khanoon, alright?
- Hello.

627
00:32:22,810 --> 00:32:24,830
It's a pleasure to meet you all.

628
00:32:24,850 --> 00:32:27,590
If you need anything,
please call me anytime.

629
00:32:27,610 --> 00:32:30,250
Alright. You can sit next to Pun.

630
00:32:30,280 --> 00:32:31,320
And...

631
00:32:32,350 --> 00:32:34,200
If you need anything,
they will assist you.

632
00:32:34,230 --> 00:32:35,680
- Alright.
- Yes.

633
00:32:37,690 --> 00:32:39,350
You can sit next to Pun.

634
00:32:39,950 --> 00:32:41,310
- Thank you.
- Hey.

635
00:32:41,910 --> 00:32:43,490
Well, he's new here.

636
00:32:43,510 --> 00:32:45,540
- That's good. Take care of him.
- It's our job to look after him.

637
00:32:45,570 --> 00:32:47,150
Not just looking after him, though.

638
00:32:47,170 --> 00:32:48,510
Since he's our newest member,

639
00:32:48,530 --> 00:32:50,380
we need to throw him a welcome party, right?

640
00:32:50,410 --> 00:32:51,320
Hey.

641
00:32:51,340 --> 00:32:53,830
That's a reasonable thing to do.

642
00:32:53,940 --> 00:32:54,840
Of course.

643
00:32:55,020 --> 00:32:56,020
What now, Sis?

644
00:32:56,610 --> 00:32:57,610
Um...

645
00:32:58,250 --> 00:33:01,960
Tonight. At the same karaoke bar
we hosted Jane's welcome party.

646
00:33:02,330 --> 00:33:04,550
- Yay!
- Yay!

647
00:33:04,570 --> 00:33:05,840
That's more like it!

648
00:33:06,040 --> 00:33:07,640
Amazing. That's the spirit.

649
00:33:08,620 --> 00:33:09,230
Jane.

650
00:33:09,250 --> 00:33:09,810
Hm?

651
00:33:09,830 --> 00:33:11,120
Help me keep the mic safe.

652
00:33:11,450 --> 00:33:13,420
Don't let Khanoon take it.

653
00:33:13,440 --> 00:33:15,440
Oh, you'll regret saying that.

654
00:33:15,650 --> 00:33:17,540
I'll be seeing you tonight, then.

655
00:33:17,560 --> 00:33:19,350
Whoa, Khanoon.
Why wait until tonight?

656
00:33:19,370 --> 00:33:21,820
- How about we settle it right here? Damn it.
- Come on, then.

657
00:33:21,840 --> 00:33:23,800
- Hey.
- Sorry, sorry, sorry.

658
00:33:24,160 --> 00:33:26,260
- Three, two, one!
- Come on.

659
00:33:26,340 --> 00:33:27,330
Just kidding.

660
00:33:27,350 --> 00:33:29,960
- Our team doesn't condone violence.
- Exactly.

661
00:33:29,980 --> 00:33:32,130
- No shit.
- We usually work hard.

662
00:33:34,810 --> 00:33:37,350
Let's grab some food at the entrance of the alley.

663
00:33:37,370 --> 00:33:39,140
If you want to have lunch there,

664
00:33:39,160 --> 00:33:41,570
or if you don't have
your own lunch with you, join us.

665
00:33:41,590 --> 00:33:42,670
- Mm.
- Okay?

666
00:33:43,370 --> 00:33:45,690
Eat up. Make sure you enjoy it, too.

667
00:33:45,720 --> 00:33:47,680
Sis is rarely this generous.

668
00:33:48,040 --> 00:33:49,430
Hey, Sis!

669
00:33:52,680 --> 00:33:54,080
It's to welcome him.

670
00:33:54,140 --> 00:33:56,980
What's wrong? Are you arguing with the fridge?

671
00:33:58,450 --> 00:33:59,450
Jane!

672
00:34:01,250 --> 00:34:02,200
What is it?

673
00:34:03,070 --> 00:34:06,160
I...want to share my fruits with Ai.

674
00:34:06,180 --> 00:34:08,680
Which one of these
do you think he will like...?

675
00:34:09,890 --> 00:34:10,890
I don't know.

676
00:34:11,190 --> 00:34:12,190
Why don't you ask him?

677
00:34:12,220 --> 00:34:13,120
Ai...

678
00:34:14,980 --> 00:34:17,440
I'm too nervous to talk to him.

679
00:34:18,070 --> 00:34:20,040
I'm afraid he wouldn't like any of these.

680
00:34:20,060 --> 00:34:21,560
I have nothing else to give him either.

681
00:34:21,870 --> 00:34:24,560
Oh, you introvert.

682
00:34:24,980 --> 00:34:26,330
I don't really get it,

683
00:34:26,360 --> 00:34:27,470
but I kinda do.

684
00:34:27,880 --> 00:34:30,040
How about this? Don't worry.

685
00:34:30,060 --> 00:34:31,320
I'll handle it for you.

686
00:34:33,890 --> 00:34:34,890
Ai.

687
00:34:34,910 --> 00:34:35,840
Yes, Jaab?

688
00:34:36,160 --> 00:34:38,960
Jane wants to share his fruits with you...

689
00:34:38,980 --> 00:34:39,880
Do you want some?

690
00:34:40,640 --> 00:34:42,930
He has mangoes,

691
00:34:42,960 --> 00:34:44,600
longans, grapes,

692
00:34:44,640 --> 00:34:45,860
apples, and guavas.

693
00:34:45,880 --> 00:34:46,460
Do you want anything?

694
00:34:46,480 --> 00:34:47,780
I can try any of them.

695
00:34:47,800 --> 00:34:48,980
I love fruits.

696
00:34:49,000 --> 00:34:50,520
Oh, so you're easy to feed.

697
00:34:53,760 --> 00:34:54,760
Let's see, Jane.

698
00:34:58,020 --> 00:34:59,500
Here. I'll help.

699
00:35:09,340 --> 00:35:10,140
Here.

700
00:35:10,740 --> 00:35:12,240
This one is all yours.

701
00:35:12,280 --> 00:35:14,560
Auntie Kaew said not to
share it with anyone.

702
00:35:18,530 --> 00:35:20,200
This looks amazing, Jane.

703
00:35:21,480 --> 00:35:22,960
Don't get ahead of yourself.

704
00:35:24,170 --> 00:35:25,680
Don't, my ass.

705
00:35:28,450 --> 00:35:30,600
Are these from your orchards?

706
00:35:30,640 --> 00:35:32,860
- Some of them are.
- Mm.

707
00:35:32,880 --> 00:35:34,470
But they're all organic.

708
00:35:34,490 --> 00:35:36,120
I got them from my fellow orchard owners.

709
00:35:36,330 --> 00:35:37,280
These are huge.

710
00:35:37,300 --> 00:35:38,580
They look amazing.

711
00:35:39,530 --> 00:35:40,840
I'm not trying to brag or anything,

712
00:35:40,860 --> 00:35:41,860
but this guy!

713
00:35:41,880 --> 00:35:43,000
The person in front of you here,

714
00:35:43,250 --> 00:35:44,910
owns the entire Phetchabun province.

715
00:35:44,930 --> 00:35:45,920
- Huh?!
- What?

716
00:35:46,550 --> 00:35:47,800
You own...

717
00:35:47,830 --> 00:35:49,400
the entire province?

718
00:35:49,540 --> 00:35:50,240
No, I don't!

719
00:35:50,270 --> 00:35:51,220
Are you part of the royal family?

720
00:35:51,240 --> 00:35:51,900
No.

721
00:35:51,920 --> 00:35:53,720
Are you from an elite clan?

722
00:35:54,760 --> 00:35:55,930
That's a good guess.

723
00:35:55,950 --> 00:35:58,400
The design of his house is like...

724
00:35:58,560 --> 00:36:00,480
You're misleading everyone, Jaab.

725
00:36:01,450 --> 00:36:04,040
I think Jane is an ordinary person.

726
00:36:04,970 --> 00:36:06,680
But he's an ordinary person who is...

727
00:36:07,160 --> 00:36:07,760
wealthy.

728
00:36:09,350 --> 00:36:10,800
It's not like that, Ai.

729
00:36:11,360 --> 00:36:13,000
Don't get me wrong.

730
00:36:13,340 --> 00:36:16,330
But if you walked in from the entrance,

731
00:36:16,350 --> 00:36:17,950
and you brought grapes with you,

732
00:36:17,970 --> 00:36:19,320
by the time you reached the actual house,

733
00:36:19,340 --> 00:36:20,800
those grapes would've already
turned into wine.

734
00:36:20,830 --> 00:36:21,910
It's so vast.

735
00:36:21,930 --> 00:36:23,030
Shit. Are you serious?

736
00:36:23,050 --> 00:36:24,320
- Really?
- Wine, you say?

737
00:36:25,460 --> 00:36:26,540
So his place is massive.

738
00:36:26,570 --> 00:36:28,840
I want to visit there now.

739
00:36:28,860 --> 00:36:30,520
Will you come? You'll have a good time.

740
00:36:30,550 --> 00:36:32,060
There are so many things to do.

741
00:36:32,090 --> 00:36:33,480
- Can I go?
- Sure.

742
00:36:34,980 --> 00:36:36,580
There's a beautiful water reservoir, too.

743
00:36:36,600 --> 00:36:39,240
The evening vibe there is amazing,
and the sunset is stunning.

744
00:36:52,160 --> 00:36:53,360
Anything I can help?

745
00:36:54,140 --> 00:36:55,140
Oh...

746
00:36:55,460 --> 00:36:56,460
Well...

747
00:36:56,660 --> 00:36:59,720
I tried to print it out.
There were some rattling noises,

748
00:36:59,740 --> 00:37:02,800
but nothing came out.

749
00:37:03,070 --> 00:37:03,960
Oh...

750
00:37:04,540 --> 00:37:05,840
The paper is probably jammed.

751
00:37:06,350 --> 00:37:07,930
Let me see what I can do.

752
00:37:07,950 --> 00:37:08,950
Sure.

753
00:37:26,350 --> 00:37:27,350
Yay!

754
00:37:27,370 --> 00:37:28,640
It worked.

755
00:37:28,740 --> 00:37:31,520
You're this happy over
something so small?

756
00:37:31,640 --> 00:37:32,400
Uh...

757
00:37:32,960 --> 00:37:33,960
Well...

758
00:37:34,060 --> 00:37:36,070
Without your help,

759
00:37:36,090 --> 00:37:38,360
I wouldn't have figured it out.

760
00:37:38,390 --> 00:37:39,800
Like...

761
00:37:40,970 --> 00:37:43,240
I didn't want to bother the others, too.

762
00:37:43,440 --> 00:37:46,150
Actually, everyone here is happy to help.

763
00:37:46,170 --> 00:37:47,600
Feel free to ask around.

764
00:37:47,860 --> 00:37:49,080
Oh.

765
00:37:50,120 --> 00:37:51,480
I'm the kindest person here, though.

766
00:37:51,970 --> 00:37:53,920
Tell me if you need help.

767
00:37:54,150 --> 00:37:56,120
Oh, it's fine.

768
00:37:56,270 --> 00:37:58,240
I'm a PD intern.

769
00:37:58,260 --> 00:38:01,120
Bew said Jane is my supervisor.

770
00:38:01,450 --> 00:38:02,240
I guess...

771
00:38:02,470 --> 00:38:04,240
PDs and PMs do pretty similar work.

772
00:38:04,470 --> 00:38:05,760
We can help each other out,

773
00:38:06,170 --> 00:38:09,120
since we sit next to each other.

774
00:38:09,690 --> 00:38:12,320
Oh. Thank you, Pun.

775
00:38:12,460 --> 00:38:13,200
And...

776
00:38:13,870 --> 00:38:15,160
how are you going to the karaoke bar?

777
00:38:15,240 --> 00:38:16,950
I'm not sure, actually.

778
00:38:16,970 --> 00:38:19,800
I think I'm gonna hitch a ride
with someone here.

779
00:38:22,740 --> 00:38:24,880
Can that someone be me?

780
00:38:25,470 --> 00:38:26,040
Yes?

781
00:38:28,250 --> 00:38:29,800
My car has some available seats.

782
00:38:30,260 --> 00:38:31,460
Several ones, actually.

783
00:38:33,250 --> 00:38:34,250
Oh.

784
00:38:37,170 --> 00:38:38,840
I'll take that smile as a yes.

785
00:38:51,660 --> 00:38:54,590
Uh... I need to get back to work now.

786
00:38:54,610 --> 00:38:55,400
Oh.

787
00:38:56,650 --> 00:38:58,550
- Sure.
- Thank you.

788
00:38:58,950 --> 00:38:59,950
Go ahead.

789
00:39:07,120 --> 00:39:08,850
One, two, three, four!
[Intern Welcome Party]

790
00:39:22,070 --> 00:39:22,960
Alright. Come on!

791
00:39:34,270 --> 00:39:35,280
Ai.

792
00:39:35,780 --> 00:39:36,600
Yes?

793
00:39:36,960 --> 00:39:38,600
How was your first day?

794
00:39:39,150 --> 00:39:40,240
Oh...

795
00:39:40,460 --> 00:39:41,460
It went well.

796
00:39:41,840 --> 00:39:44,520
Working at the office
was much more fun than I thought.

797
00:39:45,240 --> 00:39:46,720
I'm feeling less nervous now.

798
00:39:55,750 --> 00:39:57,000
Is there something on your mind, Jane?

799
00:40:01,670 --> 00:40:05,080
Jaab told me to confess.

800
00:40:06,350 --> 00:40:07,240
Huh?

801
00:40:07,740 --> 00:40:08,720
Confess?

802
00:40:16,160 --> 00:40:18,160
What do I do?

803
00:40:27,940 --> 00:40:29,470
- Ow! Ow!
- Oh?

804
00:40:29,750 --> 00:40:30,960
Was that you, Jane?

805
00:40:30,990 --> 00:40:32,060
Where are you?

806
00:40:32,080 --> 00:40:32,960
Jaab!

807
00:40:33,250 --> 00:40:34,280
- Oh!
- It hurts!

808
00:40:40,850 --> 00:40:41,880
Are you alright?

809
00:40:44,740 --> 00:40:45,680
I'm fine.

810
00:40:45,740 --> 00:40:46,680
Oh.

811
00:40:46,960 --> 00:40:49,550
You're frowning like
wilted vegetables,

812
00:40:49,570 --> 00:40:50,840
and you're telling me you're fine?

813
00:40:54,270 --> 00:40:56,360
I've never been
a supervisor before, Jaab.

814
00:40:57,260 --> 00:41:00,000
Are you...stressed about Ai?

815
00:41:00,640 --> 00:41:01,680
Mm.

816
00:41:02,840 --> 00:41:04,950
- What should I do?
- Aww...

817
00:41:05,100 --> 00:41:07,020
Come here. It's okay.

818
00:41:07,040 --> 00:41:09,050
Don't cry, Jane.

819
00:41:09,070 --> 00:41:11,560
- There, there, there.
- I'm worried he'd feel uncomfortable.

820
00:41:11,750 --> 00:41:13,480
I'm not that social.

821
00:41:14,780 --> 00:41:16,560
I'm worried he'd think that I'm strict

822
00:41:16,820 --> 00:41:18,640
and that I refuse to teach him
about work.

823
00:41:20,670 --> 00:41:22,640
How am I supposed to mentor anyone?

824
00:41:23,060 --> 00:41:24,780
I can't even take care of myself.

825
00:41:26,150 --> 00:41:27,850
How about you be direct with him?

826
00:41:27,870 --> 00:41:29,360
I think he'll understand.

827
00:41:31,320 --> 00:41:32,330
What should I tell him?

828
00:41:32,350 --> 00:41:33,670
Just tell him that

829
00:41:33,700 --> 00:41:35,280
"I'm not good at talking,

830
00:41:35,560 --> 00:41:37,470
but I'm not strict."

831
00:41:37,490 --> 00:41:38,480
Something like that.

832
00:41:38,960 --> 00:41:41,120
Whatever you think will
make him uncomfortable,

833
00:41:41,140 --> 00:41:42,760
just say it to him right away.

834
00:41:44,720 --> 00:41:46,840
